    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s not just the noise. it’s that there’s no place for someone like me anymore. i look at everything—the way people interact, the way everything is just... disposable—and i realize i’m just a relic. a leftover. like a book in a language no one speaks anymore. it's just exhausting trying to pretend i still fit in a world that has no use for me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
